# Performance & Security Hardening (Permanent)

## HTTP surface

- **CORS:** allow only `CORS_ORIGINS` (comma list); credentials on; no `*`.
- **Helmet:** enabled on Nest HTTP (secure headers). Do not disable in production for convenience.
- **Trust proxy:** when `TRUST_PROXY=true`, enable Express trust proxy so IP allowlists / rate keys see real client IPs behind reverse proxies.

## Rate limits (Redis)

| Surface | Keys / knobs |
| --- | --- |
| OTP | existing `OTP_*` |
| Share unlock | existing `SHARE_LINK_*` |
| PDF export enqueue | `EXPORT_RATE_MAX` / `EXPORT_RATE_WINDOW_SECONDS` per `businessId` |

## Export queue cost controls

- Cap **in-flight** jobs per Business: `queued` + `processing` ≤ `EXPORT_MAX_CONCURRENT_PER_BUSINESS`.
- Worker concurrency: `EXPORT_WORKER_CONCURRENCY` (default 1 — PDF is CPU/RAM heavy).
- Never run PDF render on the interactive HTTP path (editor keystroke).

## Data / indexes

- Every tenant table queried by `businessId` must keep a supporting index (usually `(businessId, …)`).
- List APIs stay paginated; no unbounded tenant scans.

## IDOR

- Path `:businessId` + membership on every tenant read/write; Mongo filters always include `businessId`.

## Forbidden

- Opening CORS to `*` with credentials.
- Unbounded concurrent PDF jobs per tenant.
- Skipping Helmet in SAAS/SELF_HOSTED production images without an ADR.
